          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            When formulating a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+physics"} theory of physics
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            one typically models the range of certain physical quantities by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsors"} torsors
            over some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of transformations.
          %p
            For instance a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavelength"} wavelength
            would be identified as an element in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+real+numbers"} positive real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\gt0}
            , being a torsor over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\gt0}^\times
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+reals"} positive reals
          %p
            In order for the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordination"}> coordination
            ” of the mathematical theory with physical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            to take place, one needs to choose an identification of this abstract torsor with the (idealized) one that it is supposed to model in nature. Such a choice is equivalent to a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            (in the mathematical sense), hence a choice of element of the torsor. In this context this is then a
            = succeed "." do
              %em physical unit
          %p
            For instance picking an element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\gt0}
            and declaring this to be the length of the path travelled by light in a vacuum in 1/299 792 458 second means defining a
            %em physical unit of length
            (in this example: of the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meter"} meter
          %p
            Notice that
            %em choice of unit
            is also called
            = succeed "." do
              %em choice of gauge
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge"} gauge
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "gauge#Weyl23"} Weyl 23
          %h2#relation_to_physical_constants Relation to physical constants
          %p
            Physical units are often called
            = succeed "." do
              %em physical constants
          %p
            The actual
            = succeed "," do
              %em constants of nature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck length
            belongs to the torsor of length, a torsor over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\gt0}^\times
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1.616
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msup
                    %mn 10
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 35
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1.616 \cdot 10^{-35} \mathrm{m}
            — but the number appearing in this statement is completely driven by our arbitrary choice of the meter.
          %p
            An actual constant of nature corresponds to a specific, non-arbitrary real number only when it is a
            %em dimensionless
            quotient of physical quantities. For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fine+structure+constant"} fine structure constant
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ≔
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 4
                      %mi π
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\alpha \coloneqq \frac{e^2}{ (4 \pi \epsilon_0) \hbar c} \in \mathbb{R}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+charge"} electric charge
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            itself, and hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            characterizing nature independently of any conventions about how to parameterize it.
          %p
            For computing such a quotient concretely, one expresses each of the constituent quantities as some real multiple of an appropriate physical unit: e.g.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            as a multiple of the
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                coulomb
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/coulomb"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            as a multiple of the meter per second, etc. If the units are chosen such that their quotient is unity, then the quotient of the numbers is the actual physical constant.
          %h2#UnitsOfLengthInLagrangianFieldTheory Units of length in Lagrangian field theory
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \simeq \mathbb{R}^{p,1}
            be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi fb
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{fb}{\to} \Sigma
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            bundle. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\phi^a\}
            for local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            on the typical fiber of this bundle.
          %p
            The total space of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi jb
                        %mn ∞
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^\infty_\Sigma(E) \overset{jb^\infty}{\to} \Sigma
            carries an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sc
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ×
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sc \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^\times \times J^\infty_\Sigma(E) \longrightarrow J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
          %p
            of the multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi μ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi r
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi μ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mi k
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                          %msup
                            %mi r
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi k
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mi k
                            %mi a
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  x^\mu &amp; \mapsto r x^\mu
                  \\\
                  \\phi^a &amp; \mapsto \phi^a
                  \\\
                  \\phi^a_{,\mu_1, \cdots \mu_k} &amp; \mapsto r^{-k} \phi^a_{,\mu_1 \cdots \mu_k}
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p Let then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{(-)}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow \mathbf{\Omega}^{p+1}(J^\infty_\Sigma(E))
          %p
            be a smoothly
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\times
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi scp
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  scp \;\colon\; \mathbb{R}^\times \times \mathbb{R}^n \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
          %p
            Observe that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equations"} Euler-Lagrange equations
            induced by a Lagrangian density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            equal those induced by the rescaled Lagrangian
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \mathbf{L}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+current"} presymplectic current
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi BFV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{BFV}
            induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            scales linearly with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            itself. Upon
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi BFV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{BFV}
            may be absorbed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
            %em homogeneously
            the rescaled Lagrangian induces the same physics.
          %p
            Hence we require that the combined scaling action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^\infty_\Sigma(E)
            via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sc
            and on the parameters in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi scp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} scp
            is homogeneous on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            in that there exists
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim \in \mathbb{Z}
            such that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}^\times
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi sc
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi scp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi dim
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sc_r^\ast \mathbf{L}_{( scp(-))} = r^{dim} \mathbf{L}_{(-)}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then a parameter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}
            such that there exists
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in \mathbb{Z}
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi scp
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi w
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  scp_r^\ast a = r^{w} a
          %p
            is said to have
            %em dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi length
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [length]^{w}
          %p
            For example the Lagrangian density for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+field+theory"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+field"} scalar field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi J
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{(-)}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  \\mathbb{R}^1
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbf{\Omega}^{p+1}(J^\infty_\Sigma(\Sigma \times \mathbb{R})
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mi m
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ,
                        %mi μ
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ν
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi m
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo )
                  %mi dvol
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{m}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  \\left(
                  \\eta^{\mu \nu}\phi_{,\mu} \phi_{,\nu}
                  \-
                  m^2 \phi^2
                  \\right)
                  dvol
          %p
            is parameterized by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^{p-1}
            the mass parameter has to have dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi length
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [length]^{-1}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℏ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m c / \hbar
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Compton+wavelength"} Compton wavelength
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi ν
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ,
                        %mi μ
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ν
                    %mo −
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mi c
                          %mi ℏ
                      %mo )
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo )
                  %mi dvol
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{L}_{m c / \hbar}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  \\left(
                  \\eta^{\mu \nu}\phi_{,\mu} \phi_{,\nu}
                  \-
                  \\left(
                  \\tfrac{m c}{\hbar}
                  \\right)
                  \\phi^2
                  \\right)
                  dvol
          %p (…)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meter"}> meter
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/femtometer"} femtometer
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electronvolt"}> electronvolt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MeV"} MeV
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GeV"} GeV
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TeV"} TeV
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boltzmann+constant"} Boltzmann constant
          %h3#scales Scales
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                fundamental
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scales"} scales
              (fundamental/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+unit"} natural
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+units"} physical units
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/speed+of+light"} speed of light
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℏ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitational+constant"} gravitational constant
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi κ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 8
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_N = \kappa^2/8\pi
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+scale"} Planck scale
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+length"} Planck length
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi ℓ
                              %mi p
                            %mo =
                            %msqrt
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℏ
                                %mi G
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %msup
                                  %mi c
                                  %mn 3
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_p = \sqrt{ \hbar G / c^3 }
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+mass"} Planck mass
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi m
                              %mi p
                            %mo =
                            %msqrt
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℏ
                                %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi G
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_p = \sqrt{\hbar c / G}
              %li
                %p
                  depending on a given
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Compton+wavelength"} Compton wavelength
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi λ
                              %mi m
                            %mo =
                            %mi ℏ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi m
                            %mi c
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_m = \hbar / m c
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwarzschild+radius"} Schwarzschild radius
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi m
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msup
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 m G / c^2
                  %li
                    %p
                      depending also on a given
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi e
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                    %ul
                      %li
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+limit"} Schwinger limit
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
